+# Corpus fetch limits
+
+`manifest.tsv` (323 entries) was fetched raw, subject to the "Svipall" per-domain
+rate limit observed while building this corpus:
+
+- **12 visits per 60 s window**, per domain.
+- **900 s cooldown** imposed after a breach of that window.
+
+This is why `GATE1.md` notes fetching is rate-limited and only 115 of 323 entries
+were on disk at measurement time, with the rest fetched incrementally.
+
+## Hosts used
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com` — primary source (see the header row of
+  `manifest.tsv`).
+- `cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/<owner>/<repo>@<branch>/<path>` — mirror.
+- `cdn.statically.io` — mirror; observed to be slow / prone to timeouts.
+
+`out_file` for fetched content landed flat in `~/.svipall/out/`.
+
+Note: these figures come from this project's own session record (a trust-1,
+tool-observed Muninn episode), not from a config file checked into this repo —
+no fetch script or rate-limit config was found in the repository itself.
